terraform init: Run this first in every new Terraform project.

terraform validate: Checks Terraform syntax.
                    Verifies configuration is valid.

terraform fmt -recursive: Automatically formats .tf files
                          Makes code readable and standardized

terraform plan: Shows what Terraform will create/update/delete
                Does not make actual changes

terraform apply: Creates or updates infrastructure
terraform apply -auto-approve

terraform destroy: Deletes all infrastructure managed by Terraform
terraform destroy -auto-approve

terraform show: Displays Terraform state details

terraform state list: Shows all tracked resources

terraform import <resource_type.name> <resource_id>: Brings existing cloud resources 
                                                     under Terraform management
terraform import aws_s3_bucket.demo my-bucket

terraform workspace list: Shows available environments/workspaces
terraform workspace new dev: Creates separate environment state
terraform workspace select prod: Switches environment

terraform init -upgrade: Updates provider plugins to latest allowed versions
terraform providers lock: Creates dependency lock file

terraform refresh: Updates Terraform state from real infrastructure

| File               | Purpose                |
| ------------------ | ---------------------- |
| `main.tf`          | Main configuration     |
| `variables.tf`     | Input variables        |
| `outputs.tf`       | Output values          |
| `terraform.tfvars` | Variable values        |
| `providers.tf`     | Provider configuration |
| `backend.tf`       | Remote state config    |
